MID_EV13_036_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_036_m01_001: Your Majesty, I've received details of our next\nscheduled match.
MID_EV13_036_m01_002: Tell me, and include any research you've\nconducted on our opponent.
MID_EV13_036_m01_003: <TLP>Megaira's Beacon\n\nMatch: Third Qualifier of the Heroic Games\nOpponent: Silver Knights of Tellus\nLeader: Alexandra\n\nDate: {DateTime=Month} {DateTime=Day}
MID_EV13_036_m01_004: I've heard of this Alexandra in passing.
MID_EV13_036_m01_005: They say she comes from nobility and is a crowd\nfavorite here in Dagsion.
MID_EV13_036_m01_006: Oh, she's a noble too? Not that I'd know her, I guess.
MID_EV13_036_m01_007: Interestingly, this maiden we face next has not yet\nfought in the tournament.
MID_EV13_036_m01_008: How is that possible?
MID_EV13_036_m01_009: To be clear, she has had matches, but she has won\nall of them up to now by default.
MID_EV13_036_m01_010: Huh, that's weird. She must be one lucky gal.
MID_EV13_036_m01_011: I'm not the only one who thinks that's fishy, right?\nShe's gotta be cheating.
MID_EV13_036_m01_012: She may try something between now and the match.\nLet us be on our guard.
MID_EV13_036_m01_013: By the way...if I might venture onto some well-\nworn territory for a moment...
MID_EV13_036_m01_014: If this is another plea for me to take a husband or\nproduce an heir, then make it brief.
MID_EV13_036_m01_015: It is not the first time I have heard from you on the\nsubject, and I doubt it will be the last.
MID_EV13_036_m01_016: I find a ruler not of Your Majesty's line to\nbe unacceptable.
MID_EV13_036_m01_017: I am aware that saying so is above my station,\nbut I would be displeased with anything less.
MID_EV13_036_m01_018: Your stance is noted. But can you not respect my\nown preferences?
MID_EV13_036_m01_019: I have exacting criteria for any who would be my\nlifelong partner.
MID_EV13_036_m01_020: As to an heir, anyone qualified will do in the end,\nregardless of their bloodline.
MID_EV13_036_m01_021: Tell the chancellor to keep his eye out for\noutstanding candidates within Saramis.
MID_EV13_036_m01_022: Your Majesty, that may play into the hands of the\nDyan faction, who insist that the bloodline is all.
MID_EV13_036_m01_023: He may have disappeared from public view, but he\nstill has support among the people.
MID_EV13_036_m01_024: I promise that once our work here is concluded,\nI will take up this matter in earnest.
MID_EV13_036_m01_025: Our search for an heir is a last resort only. For now,\nI wish to focus on the tournament.
MID_EV13_036_m01_026: Thank you.
MID_EV13_036_m01_027: <NCA>Bring up Dyan.
MID_EV13_036_m01_028: When the Heroic Games are over, my first priority\nwill be to put an end to Dyan.
MID_EV13_036_m01_029: What?! Actually...that may be for the best.
MID_EV13_036_m01_030: Perhaps I truly ought to sever the Savangren line\nand leave the throne to new blood.
MID_EV13_036_m01_031: What am I hearing?! I won't have it. I have served\nthe royal family since the late king.
MID_EV13_036_m01_032: And I intend to serve until I see your child's face.\nNay, until that child's wedding! Nay, further!
MID_EV13_036_m01_033: I will see that child's child born! Such is the extent\nof my devotion.
MID_EV13_036_m01_034: <NCA>Express your exasperation.
MID_EV13_036_m01_035: How long can one man live? Be sensible. You've\nserved long enough already.
MID_EV13_036_m01_036: But it is only by rallying around Your Majesty that\nSaramis remains united.
MID_EV13_036_m01_037: There is no other potential heir who would satisfy\nall factions as you do.
MID_EV13_036_m01_038: More likely, the kingdom would fall into civil war\nover the throne.
MID_EV13_036_m01_039: A child of your line, however, would be accepted\nby all.
MID_EV13_036_m01_040: Forgive me, Your Majesty, but is there anything\nelse that troubles you?
MID_EV13_036_m01_041: Nothing you need concern yourself with.\nNow leave me.
MID_EV13_036_m01_042: There is not much time left for me to do as you\nwish, Bonaventure.
MID_EV13_036_m01_043: Perhaps at some point in the next seven years.\nThough I have much to do before then.
MID_EV13_038_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_038_m01_001: Boss, what the hell was that?
MID_EV13_038_m01_002: I assumed you had been irritable lately due to\nthe heavy burden of the crown.
MID_EV13_038_m01_003: But what I saw today was something else. You were\nlike a woman possessed.
MID_EV13_038_m01_004: Have you been hiding something from us, boss?
MID_EV13_038_m01_005: Some kinda secret you didn't even wanna let us\nin on?
MID_EV13_038_m01_006: <NCA>Tell them about the 10-year limit.
MID_EV13_038_m01_007: <NCB>Tell them about the warding chain.
MID_EV13_038_m01_008: <ACA>There is no hiding it from you any longer, I see.
MID_EV13_038_m01_009: <ACA>Troy told me I have, at most, 10 years. Something\nof a side effect of this arm.
MID_EV13_038_m01_010: <ACA>Ten years to what? The arm rots off?
MID_EV13_038_m01_011: <ACA>Not my arm, but my mind. It was Mahadu's\ndownfall as well.
MID_EV13_038_m01_012: <ACA>And this is how I am faring after a mere 3 years,\nlet alone 10.
MID_EV13_038_m01_013: <ACB>The arm is slowly consuming my mind. It was\nMahadu's downfall as well.
MID_EV13_038_m01_014: <ACB>I have kept the arm's curse at bay with this\nwarding chain—an amulet Troy gave me.
MID_EV13_038_m01_015: <ACB>But it shattered during our decisive battle\nwith Bahr Vahn.
MID_EV13_038_m01_016: <ACB>Ever since, whenever I use the arm's power,\nI hear a strange voice.
MID_EV13_038_m01_017: <ACB>It echoes from the depths of the earth and bids me\nto destroy everything.
MID_EV13_038_m01_018: I can't believe this.
MID_EV13_038_m01_019: Why did you not confide in us before?
MID_EV13_038_m01_020: I had a dream. Something I needed to achieve as\nqueen no matter the cost.
MID_EV13_038_m01_021: When I lost my arm, that dream was closed off\nto me. I felt as though I might as well be dead.
MID_EV13_038_m01_022: Then I learned that I could have an extra 10 years.
MID_EV13_038_m01_023: The dead end was opened anew by a beckoning\ngleam. I chose it without hesitation.
MID_EV13_038_m01_024: I swore to use all my strength to see the dream to\nfruition, even if it meant my own ruin.
MID_EV13_038_m01_025: This whole time, you've sat on the throne of\nSaramis bearing such weight.
MID_EV13_038_m01_026: I was a fool. I am ashamed to admit I never grasped\nthe enormity of your will.
MID_EV13_038_m01_027: I still don't. Why do you want to be queen so bad?
MID_EV13_038_m01_028: Lilian! You speak out of turn.
MID_EV13_038_m01_029: No, really, why do something that's gonna destroy\nyou in the end? Just let Dyan have the throne.
MID_EV13_038_m01_030: Are you trying to live up to your father's\nexpectations? To your reputation? What?
MID_EV13_038_m01_031: Neither. One might say...I am trying to live up to\nmy duty.
MID_EV13_038_m01_032: If you say so.
MID_EV13_038_m01_033: Boss, we could just rip the arm off right here.
MID_EV13_038_m01_034: And in so doing, forfeit my right to the throne.\nThat does nothing to serve my people.
MID_EV13_038_m01_035: Alright then. I got a pretty good idea of where\nyour head's at now, boss.
MID_EV13_038_m01_036: We'll back you up down the line. So don't give in to\nthat messed-up arm!
MID_EV13_038_m01_037: Just so. I vow to devote even more of my attention\nto you, Your Majesty.
MID_EV13_038_m01_038: Y'see, boss? I can't promise anything, but I\nguarantee everything'll be fine!
MID_EV13_038_m01_039: Thank you... All of you.